WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:01.826
- Good morning believe nation, it's Evan.

00:00:01.826 --> 00:00:04.505
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.277
more than they believe in themselves.

00:00:06.277 --> 00:00:08.748
And my sincere hope is
that if you see in yourself

00:00:08.748 --> 00:00:12.278
what I see in you, you'll be
able to change the planet.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.187
So to help you on your
journey today's message

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:16.972
is be who you were born to be.

00:00:16.972 --> 00:00:18.829
Over to you, Michael Jordan.

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:20.749
(rooster crowing)

00:00:20.749 --> 00:00:23.198
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:23.198 --> 00:00:25.962
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:25.962 --> 00:00:29.462
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:31.417 --> 00:00:34.129
- [Michael] It's not about the shoes.

00:00:34.129 --> 00:00:38.007
(light, peaceful piano music)

00:00:38.007 --> 00:00:41.214
It's about knowing where you're going.

00:00:41.214 --> 00:00:43.964
Not forgetting where you started.

00:00:45.586 --> 00:00:48.439
(moves to stronger,
inspirational piano music)

00:00:48.439 --> 00:00:51.606
It's about having the courage to fail.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:57.363
Not breaking when you are broken.

00:00:57.363 --> 00:01:00.280
Taking everything you've been given

00:01:01.245 --> 00:01:03.578
and making something better.

00:01:04.847 --> 00:01:06.097
It's about work

00:01:07.961 --> 00:01:09.044
before glory.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:13.323
And what's inside of you.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.796
It's doing what they say you can't.

00:01:17.796 --> 00:01:21.963
It's not about the shoes, it's
about what you do in them.

00:01:23.306 --> 00:01:25.375
It's about being

00:01:25.375 --> 00:01:27.677
who you were born to be.

00:01:27.677 --> 00:01:30.445
- Michael Jordan did
what he was born to do.

00:01:30.445 --> 00:01:32.402
He found what he was born to do

00:01:32.402 --> 00:01:34.922
and the unique thing
about it was he found it

00:01:34.922 --> 00:01:36.265
and then he actually took action on it

00:01:36.265 --> 00:01:37.262
and he worked hard at it.

00:01:37.262 --> 00:01:39.447
It wasn't just, "I'm
naturally gifted at this,

00:01:39.447 --> 00:01:42.997
"and so I can coast and
achieve some kind of results."

00:01:42.997 --> 00:01:46.155
He took the work to find the
thing that he was great at

00:01:46.155 --> 00:01:48.659
and he put in the effort
consistently to become

00:01:48.659 --> 00:01:52.172
an icon at his chosen profession.

00:01:52.172 --> 00:01:54.022
And it's great and we look up to him

00:01:54.022 --> 00:01:57.066
and I use Michael Jordan as an
example in a lot of my videos

00:01:57.066 --> 00:01:59.906
and he is perhaps the
greatest basketball player

00:01:59.906 --> 00:02:01.673
of all time.

00:02:01.673 --> 00:02:03.869
But you are no less an icon,

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:07.094
you are no less great at something.

00:02:07.094 --> 00:02:09.482
I believe that we all have
Michael Jordan level talent

00:02:09.482 --> 00:02:11.580
at something and that's
what you need to find.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:13.270
And you either haven't
found it yet because

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.002
you haven't done enough exploring to find

00:02:15.002 --> 00:02:16.568
the thing that you're great at,

00:02:16.568 --> 00:02:18.052
or you haven't put in the effort to get

00:02:18.052 --> 00:02:19.434
really, really good at it.

00:02:19.434 --> 00:02:22.034
You have this thing that
you have potential to be

00:02:22.034 --> 00:02:24.301
the Michael Jordan of in your field

00:02:24.301 --> 00:02:26.091
and you're kind of coasting on it,

00:02:26.091 --> 00:02:27.024
you're not putting in the work,

00:02:27.024 --> 00:02:28.873
you're not practicing your job shot

00:02:28.873 --> 00:02:31.389
and your free throws
and getting to the gym,

00:02:31.389 --> 00:02:34.099
whatever that equivalent
is in your industry.

00:02:34.099 --> 00:02:35.366
I like to say that Michael Jordan is not

00:02:35.366 --> 00:02:37.935
the greatest basketball player
of all time as an example.

00:02:37.935 --> 00:02:40.043
And they say the greatest
basketball player of all time

00:02:40.043 --> 00:02:41.855
was a manager at Starbucks.

00:02:41.855 --> 00:02:44.579
Because that person, that guy at Starbucks

00:02:44.579 --> 00:02:46.729
who's a manager now,

00:02:46.729 --> 00:02:48.840
should have played
basketball but he either

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:51.433
never picked up a ball,
he never explored enough

00:02:51.433 --> 00:02:54.267
to find out what he was great
at, or he never practiced.

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.490
And I think if you
don't know what you have

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.126
Michael Jordan level talent at,

00:02:58.126 --> 00:02:59.552
then you need to explore.

00:02:59.552 --> 00:03:01.802
So often we discount things

00:03:03.274 --> 00:03:07.731
that could immensely serve
us without even trying.

00:03:07.731 --> 00:03:10.365
Because it goes against our culture,

00:03:10.365 --> 00:03:12.522
it goes against how we,
you know what was on

00:03:12.522 --> 00:03:13.867
our radar at the start.

00:03:13.867 --> 00:03:16.343
Like I never thought I was
going to be an entrepreneur.

00:03:16.343 --> 00:03:18.038
I just didn't have
entrepreneurs in my family,

00:03:18.038 --> 00:03:21.001
we didn't talk about
entrepreneurship growing up.

00:03:21.001 --> 00:03:23.000
It wasn't something that
was ever on my radar.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.538
And so I never thought I was
going to be an entrepreneur.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:28.382
And I had the good fortune to
connect with two entrepreneurs

00:03:28.382 --> 00:03:30.148
at the university

00:03:30.148 --> 00:03:32.659
and join their business
and be an owner in that

00:03:32.659 --> 00:03:33.993
and learn about entrepreneurship.

00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:35.352
Even though I had all these entrepreneur

00:03:35.352 --> 00:03:37.100
tendencies growing up.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.849
And I would be probably
working at some bank

00:03:38.849 --> 00:03:40.266
and hating my job if I didn't go down

00:03:40.266 --> 00:03:42.026
that entrepreneurial path.

00:03:42.026 --> 00:03:43.466
I would be the

00:03:43.466 --> 00:03:46.439
manager at Starbucks instead
of being the entrepreneur

00:03:46.439 --> 00:03:48.168
that I want to be.

00:03:48.168 --> 00:03:50.081
And so if you don't know
what you are great at,

00:03:50.081 --> 00:03:51.866
you don't know what you have
that genius level talent at

00:03:51.866 --> 00:03:54.624
then you need to go and
start to explore, try stuff!

00:03:54.624 --> 00:03:57.438
Say yes, when somebody
invites you to something,

00:03:57.438 --> 00:03:59.103
say yes and go do it!

00:03:59.103 --> 00:04:00.552
Instead of coming up with all the reasons

00:04:00.552 --> 00:04:01.869
why it's never going to work out,

00:04:01.869 --> 00:04:04.255
all the reasons why that
it's not a good fit for you,

00:04:04.255 --> 00:04:05.326
just say yes and try it.

00:04:05.326 --> 00:04:07.959
How many times have you
discounted something

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:10.757
in your head, 'cause you've
run through the analysis

00:04:10.757 --> 00:04:12.466
without ever actually taking action

00:04:12.466 --> 00:04:14.279
and saying yes to something.

00:04:14.279 --> 00:04:17.407
So if you're insanely
happy, life is amazing,

00:04:17.407 --> 00:04:19.511
you have the career you
want and the life you want

00:04:19.511 --> 00:04:21.283
the friends you want
and the family you want,

00:04:21.283 --> 00:04:22.668
everything is amazing great,

00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:24.019
you don't have to do any of this.

00:04:24.019 --> 00:04:26.332
Keep doing what you're doing,
'cause life is amazing.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.054
But if you're not happy,

00:04:28.054 --> 00:04:30.605
if you haven't found the
thing that you love yet,

00:04:30.605 --> 00:04:31.707
if your relationship isn't perfect

00:04:31.707 --> 00:04:34.402
and your business isn't perfect then

00:04:34.402 --> 00:04:37.263
you are daily unhappy, don't
sit there and complain,

00:04:37.263 --> 00:04:40.044
and don't sit there and just dismiss ideas

00:04:40.044 --> 00:04:41.608
that can help you grow,

00:04:41.608 --> 00:04:43.419
because it might be
scary or new and foreign

00:04:43.419 --> 00:04:44.735
or different to you.

00:04:44.735 --> 00:04:47.462
Just say yes and try it.

00:04:47.462 --> 00:04:49.117
Don't be that manager at Starbucks

00:04:49.117 --> 00:04:50.553
who never picked up the basketball

00:04:50.553 --> 00:04:52.033
and could have been the
greatest basketball player

00:04:52.033 --> 00:04:53.310
of all time.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.869
Be Michael Jordan.

00:04:54.869 --> 00:04:56.104
Explore.

00:04:56.104 --> 00:04:56.937
(digital swish)

00:04:56.937 --> 00:04:57.770
Say yes.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:58.632
Try it.

00:04:58.632 --> 00:04:59.601
See if it makes you come alive.

00:04:59.601 --> 00:05:01.664
If it does do it again, if not stop it

00:05:01.664 --> 00:05:03.182
and go do something else.

00:05:03.182 --> 00:05:05.784
You have Michael Jordan
level talent at something.

00:05:05.784 --> 00:05:07.057
And I want you to find it.

00:05:07.057 --> 00:05:07.890
(digital swoosh)

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.067
So the question of the day today is,

00:05:09.067 --> 00:05:11.224
(sighs) do you know what
you have Michael Jordan

00:05:11.224 --> 00:05:12.876
level talent at?

00:05:12.876 --> 00:05:15.167
And if you do, what is it?

00:05:15.167 --> 00:05:16.238
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:05:16.238 --> 00:05:17.804
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:17.804 --> 00:05:19.679
Also if you leave a
comment within the first

00:05:19.679 --> 00:05:21.491
couple hours of this video
you have a good chance

00:05:21.491 --> 00:05:23.955
of winning one of our two daily prizes.

00:05:23.955 --> 00:05:26.665
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Riccardo Garegnani,

00:05:26.665 --> 00:05:28.858
thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:05:28.858 --> 00:05:30.376
Your One Word, it really, really means

00:05:30.376 --> 00:05:32.908
a lot to me man and I hope
you're enjoying the read.

00:05:32.908 --> 00:05:33.766
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.161
I believe in you.

00:05:35.161 --> 00:05:37.065
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:05:37.065 --> 00:05:39.871
and whatever your one word is, much love

00:05:39.871 --> 00:05:41.478
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

00:05:41.478 --> 00:05:44.069
for another shot of Espresso.

00:05:44.069 --> 00:05:46.625
♫ I wake every morning

00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:50.426
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:50.426 --> 00:05:53.178
(typewriter clicking)

00:05:53.178 --> 00:05:55.853
- Nothing fails like success.

00:05:55.853 --> 00:05:57.748
You're successful, maybe
it's in your health,

00:05:57.748 --> 00:06:00.053
maybe it's in your finances,
maybe it's in your career,

00:06:00.053 --> 00:06:01.868
maybe it's in your family life.

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:04.214
Maybe it's in the way that
you show up in the world.

00:06:04.214 --> 00:06:05.047
Awesome!

00:06:05.047 --> 00:06:08.334
You're in a really
vulnerable place right now.

00:06:08.334 --> 00:06:10.518
It is one thing to be successful,

00:06:10.518 --> 00:06:13.280
it is another thing to sustain success

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.098
over the coming decades.

00:06:15.098 --> 00:06:17.161
Is that not a powerful idea?

00:06:17.161 --> 00:06:20.543
I mean, let's go to the
entertainment industry.

00:06:20.543 --> 00:06:22.542
It's very hard to be a one hit wonder,

00:06:22.542 --> 00:06:25.490
let's not knock a one hit wonder.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:29.295
But it's even harder to
become an iconic rock band

00:06:29.295 --> 00:06:30.628
or hip hop band.

00:06:32.011 --> 00:06:33.587
Let's go to the arts.

00:06:33.587 --> 00:06:37.754
It is very hard to come up with
your Sistine Chapel, got it.

00:06:39.109 --> 00:06:42.987
It is even harder to
become a Michael Angelo.

00:06:42.987 --> 00:06:44.688
So are you playing the short game?

00:06:44.688 --> 00:06:45.924
Or are you playing the long game?

00:06:45.924 --> 00:06:48.917
This is rule number two, you
know or lesson number two

00:06:48.917 --> 00:06:50.050
that life has taught me.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.067
Play the long game.

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:54.040
Aim for legendary.

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:56.971
Don't just say I want to be world class

00:06:56.971 --> 00:07:00.103
in my dominant pursuit for
a little window of time.

00:07:00.103 --> 00:07:03.069
I want to have the guts and the grit

00:07:03.069 --> 00:07:06.950
and the acumen and the
mindset and the capability

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:08.719
and the commitment to

00:07:08.719 --> 00:07:10.525
create enduring success.

00:07:10.525 --> 00:07:13.285
And that's why I say
nothing fails like success.

00:07:13.285 --> 00:07:15.674
You look at the restaurant that is hot

00:07:15.674 --> 00:07:17.322
in your neighborhood right now.

00:07:17.322 --> 00:07:19.503
They're on the path to
obsolescence if they're

00:07:19.503 --> 00:07:21.107
not really careful.

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:25.194
Sure, they went from a
little neighborhood shop

00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:27.177
that made beautiful pasta,

00:07:27.177 --> 00:07:29.073
that had great service,

00:07:29.073 --> 00:07:32.000
that had the owner on the
floor shaking your hand,

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.692
getting to know your name.

00:07:33.692 --> 00:07:35.919
Then they got written up in the magazines

00:07:35.919 --> 00:07:38.560
and then they got interviewed
and then word of mouth

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.482
spread like wildfire and what happened?

00:07:41.482 --> 00:07:42.818
They became arrogant.

00:07:42.818 --> 00:07:45.293
You see success can be so toxic.

00:07:45.293 --> 00:07:48.799
And it happens, it is such
a pull on every human being.

00:07:48.799 --> 00:07:51.108
It just plays with your mind.

00:07:51.108 --> 00:07:55.315
And you literally shift
from humility to arrogance.

00:07:55.315 --> 00:07:56.925
You shift from humility to arrogance

00:07:56.925 --> 00:07:59.232
and once the arrogance
sets in in a mindset

00:07:59.232 --> 00:08:02.035
it starts to populate every
other person on the team,

00:08:02.035 --> 00:08:03.516
every other person in the culture,

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.531
every other person in the community.

00:08:05.531 --> 00:08:07.707
And it is a very short fall

00:08:07.707 --> 00:08:10.040
from success to irrelevance.

00:08:10.985 --> 00:08:13.830
So lesson number two is
nothing fails like success

00:08:13.830 --> 00:08:17.135
as you become more successful,
become more humble.

00:08:17.135 --> 00:08:19.699
As you become more
successful, work even harder.

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:21.974
As you become more
successful, care even more

00:08:21.974 --> 00:08:23.376
about your product.

00:08:23.376 --> 00:08:26.958
As you become more
successful, learn even more.

00:08:26.958 --> 00:08:30.756
I invite you when you are
the titan of your industry

00:08:30.756 --> 00:08:34.549
be sitting in the room with 18 year olds

00:08:34.549 --> 00:08:36.777
beginning their game.

00:08:36.777 --> 00:08:38.460
When you are the,

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:41.796
the icon of your field,
be the person who is up,

00:08:41.796 --> 00:08:43.220
not at five o'clock anymore,

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:45.564
let's play at four o'clock, reading,

00:08:45.564 --> 00:08:48.657
listening to the podcast,
writing in your journal,

00:08:48.657 --> 00:08:51.642
setting your goals,
focusing on your intentions.

00:08:51.642 --> 00:08:54.902
As you become more
successful, be more humble.

00:08:54.902 --> 00:08:58.072
As you become more successful,
be even more punctual.

00:08:58.072 --> 00:09:01.324
As you become more successful,
become even more passionate.

00:09:01.324 --> 00:09:04.503
As you become older, become even younger.

00:09:04.503 --> 00:09:06.154
Yesterday I was walking on the street

00:09:06.154 --> 00:09:08.342
and I met this man in his 80s.

00:09:08.342 --> 00:09:10.316
He said, "Robin I finally retired."

00:09:10.316 --> 00:09:11.591
He's probably close to 90.

00:09:11.591 --> 00:09:12.424
And he is

00:09:13.699 --> 00:09:17.683
a legendary clothier in
the country that I live in.

00:09:17.683 --> 00:09:18.576
And he just retired.

00:09:18.576 --> 00:09:20.091
And he started his shop,

00:09:20.091 --> 00:09:22.892
which is now an empire, in 1954.

00:09:22.892 --> 00:09:23.780
So I don't know what that is,

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:25.784
but that is decades
and decades and decades

00:09:25.784 --> 00:09:28.999
and decades and he did not want to retire.

00:09:28.999 --> 00:09:31.220
He just retired, but he is still on fire

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:32.994
to do amazing things.

00:09:32.994 --> 00:09:35.672
Age is just a number,
do not let an old person

00:09:35.672 --> 00:09:38.380
into your body, nothing
fails like success.

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:40.445
- I started actually writing
a science fiction novel

00:09:40.445 --> 00:09:43.118
that had been an idea I'd
been playing with a long time,

00:09:43.118 --> 00:09:44.496
a book called Avalon.

00:09:44.496 --> 00:09:49.367
And I was working on Avalon
and it was coming pretty well.

00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:51.429
And suddenly the first chapter of

00:09:51.429 --> 00:09:53.035
Game of Thrones came to me.

00:09:53.035 --> 00:09:55.705
Where they find the dire wolf pups.

00:09:55.705 --> 00:09:58.538
(water sploshing)

00:10:05.801 --> 00:10:06.884
- It's freak.

00:10:08.964 --> 00:10:10.836
- It's a dire wolf.

00:10:10.836 --> 00:10:12.013
- I know it wasn't a part
of the science fiction

00:10:12.013 --> 00:10:15.309
novel I was writing, this was
clearly a fantasy, medieval.

00:10:15.309 --> 00:10:16.790
Had these,

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:18.937
wolves and this large family.

00:10:18.937 --> 00:10:20.787
I'd been reading a lot
of historical fiction

00:10:20.787 --> 00:10:23.389
and it might have been
in the back of my mind.

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:25.909
But suddenly it all gelled and I wrote

00:10:25.909 --> 00:10:28.113
and I wrote that chapter
in like two or three days.

00:10:28.113 --> 00:10:30.211
It just came to pour out of me.

00:10:30.211 --> 00:10:31.294
- Lord Stark.

00:10:32.945 --> 00:10:35.795
Here are five pups.
(pups squealing)

00:10:35.795 --> 00:10:38.633
One for each of the Stark children.

00:10:38.633 --> 00:10:41.304
The dire wolf is the sigil of your house.

00:10:41.304 --> 00:10:43.721
They were meant to have them.

00:10:45.011 --> 00:10:47.093
- You will train them yourselves.

00:10:47.093 --> 00:10:49.156
You'll feed them yourselves.
(metal scrapes)

00:10:49.156 --> 00:10:53.210
And if they die, you'll
bury them yourselves.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.146
- When I did return to books.

00:10:55.146 --> 00:10:56.875
I said to myself, "Okay,

00:10:56.875 --> 00:11:00.373
"I've had many things option
they never make them."

00:11:00.373 --> 00:11:03.343
I've done pilots and TV
shows, tried to keep them

00:11:03.343 --> 00:11:05.702
within budget and produceable
and they never make that.

00:11:05.702 --> 00:11:07.852
I'm tired of playing that game.

00:11:07.852 --> 00:11:09.226
You know I have a big imagination,

00:11:09.226 --> 00:11:11.288
I have an epic story I want to tell.

00:11:11.288 --> 00:11:13.384
I'm going to make it as
big as my imagination,

00:11:13.384 --> 00:11:16.556
I'm going to have all the
castles and battles I want,

00:11:16.556 --> 00:11:18.079
I'm going to have hundreds of characters,

00:11:18.079 --> 00:11:20.101
'cause the real world
is complex and I want my

00:11:20.101 --> 00:11:22.327
fictional world to be complex, too,

00:11:22.327 --> 00:11:24.305
not as a kind of simplified thing.

00:11:24.305 --> 00:11:26.089
I want to have giant
battles, I want to have

00:11:26.089 --> 00:11:28.356
incredible castles that

00:11:28.356 --> 00:11:29.662
each one is distinct from the other

00:11:29.662 --> 00:11:31.349
that people will remember for all time.

00:11:31.349 --> 00:11:33.679
I want to have dragons and dire wolves

00:11:33.679 --> 00:11:37.877
and mammoths and a wall of
ice that's 700 feet tall.

00:11:37.877 --> 00:11:40.596
I want something huge and epic that can

00:11:40.596 --> 00:11:42.410
stand up there with Tolkien.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.164
(epic orchestral music)

